August 03 2004
by Christophe Guillemin
France's number one chain flogs Mandrakesoft-equipped PCs

France's number one supermarket chain, Carrefour, has launched a pilot
project to sell PCs that come equipped with an OS not often sold by the
retail big boys - Mandrake Linux.

Called "Compubox" by the supermarket, the PC is available from Carrefour's
internet site to shoppers from France, Belgium, Luxembourg and Monaco, with
the machines rumoured to be sold in one or two Carrefour stores from
August....

Christophe Guillemin writes for ZDNet France

http://hardware.silicon.com/desktops/0,39024645,39122827,00.htm

