Hi,

If you have the fantastic book from NoStarch called "Programming Linux
Games" (Loki Software + John R. Hall, ISBN 1-886411-49-2) and have
downloaded the source from their website, you will have had no end of
problems getting the code to compile cleanly, if indeed at all!

Help is at hand!

I have now updated the source code so that everything will compile
cleanly and in some cases, actually compile!

The files can be found at

http://www.all-the-johnsons.co.uk/linux/plg.html

along with a brief changelog.

Prerequisites
-------------

1. gcc 2.95 or above
2. libsndfile
3. OpenAL
4. SDL
5. tcl 8.3 or above

Makefiles are provided for all sections except for the SDL example code.

Notes
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D

Though I have contacted NoStarch to ask for their permission to put the
code up (more as a courtesy as the code is covered by the GPL), the
material I have put on my site contains no warranty for suitability,
stability or anything else like that. The code has been compiled and
runs under Fedora Core 2, FC3 (test1) and Slackware 10.

If NoStarch request, I will remove the code from my site.

Enjoy

TTFN

Paul
